ations against Miller, could shift this either way.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 60 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Max Miller (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ohio's 7th District pairs a Republican-leaning electorate with an incumbent, Max Miller, whose race has been upended by resurfaced abuse allegations and a barrage of attack ads from both sides. Challenger Brian Poindexter, a former Brook Park council member, has raised over $600,000 with outside support, while Miller holds a large cash advantage but faces outside spending against him.\n\nMost analysts rate the race a Tossup, though two have moved it toward Democrats, and prediction markets strongly favor Poindexter. The available polls are older and sponsored by partisan groups, so the true state of the race is uncertain. Affordability and workers' rights have dominated the closing message battle in local coverage.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6543, "margin": 2.32}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7013, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7273, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7059, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6482, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6734, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7173, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6921, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.668, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7065, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7068, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7225, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7456, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6304, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6302, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6563, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6248, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6247, "margin": 2.5}]}